E["npc:ringo"] = {t="npc",n="Ringo",z="ungoro",s="Inside a cave on Fire Plume Ridge, Ringo lies overcome by heat. The goblin explorer climbed partway up Un'Goro Crater's active volcano before collapsing. His friend Spraggle Frock waits at Marshal's Refuge, worried for him.",h="Inside a cave on Fire Plume Ridge, Ringo lies overcome by heat.",sec={{t="A Venture Too Close to the Flame",b="Goblins brave dangerous places for wealth or oddities, yet Fire Plume Ridge is harsh even for them. The active volcano rises in the center of Un'Goro Crater. It spews ash, magma, and boiling steam.\n\nRingo climbed about halfway up its southern face before the suffocating heat overcame him. He left his belongings scattered outside a cave, then crawled inside for shelter. Heat exhaustion left him unable to move.",sp=0},{t="A Grueling Trek Down the Slopes",b="The journey down the mountain is an ordeal for Ringo. Dehydration and heatstroke leave him so weak that he faints again and again on the descent. Splashes from a canteen, or sometimes a brisk slap, wake him.\n\nThe route to Marshal's Refuge passes volatile elementals and predators. The escort must stay alert until Ringo can reunite with Spraggle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ringo?",a="Ringo is a goblin explorer in Un'Goro Crater. He climbed Fire Plume Ridge and collapsed from heat exhaustion inside a cave.",al={"ringo","who is ringo","ringo goblin"}},{q="Where is Ringo located?",a="Ringo lies in a south-facing cave about halfway up Fire Plume Ridge, in the center of Un'Goro Crater.",al={"ringo location","where is ringo","find ringo"}},{q="Who is looking for Ringo?",a="Spraggle Frock, Ringo's good friend at Marshal's Refuge in northern Un'Goro, is deeply worried about his disappearance.",al={"who is spraggle","ringo friend","spraggle frock"}},{q="Why keeps fainting on the way down?",a="Volcanic heat and fumes have left Ringo severely exhausted and dehydrated, so he keeps fainting. Spraggle's canteen is needed to wake him when he passes out.",al={"why does ringo faint","ringo passing out","ringo collapses"}},{q="What is Ringo's Sack?",a="Ringo's Sack is his personal pack. He left it just outside the cave when the heat overcame him and he retreated inside.",al={"ringo's sack","ringo bag","lost bag ringo"}},{q="Where does Ringo need to go?",a="Ringo needs an escort off the volcano and across the crater floor to Marshal's Refuge. His friend Spraggle Frock is waiting there.",al={"where do i take ringo","ringo destination","ringo escort end"}}},kw={"fire plume ridge","goblin","heat exhaustion","marshal's refuge","ringo","spraggle frock","un'goro crater"},rel={"subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:marshal-s-refuge","zone:ungoro","topic:goblin"},src={"Ringo"}}
E["npc:torwa-pathfinder"] = {t="npc",n="Torwa Pathfinder",z="ungoro",s="At Un'Goro Crater's entrance, Torwa Pathfinder watches and tracks the wilds. The lone tauren hunter camps below the ramp from Tanaris, studying the basin's primordial wildlife and dangerous predators. Adventurers who seek to test themselves against its legendary beasts come to him for guidance.",h="At Un'Goro Crater's entrance, Torwa Pathfinder watches and tracks the wilds.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Threshold",b="Torwa Pathfinder camps at the crater's eastern base, where Tanaris's desert gives way to jungle. He respects Un'Goro's wild forces and watches newcomers in his own way, knowing careless wanderers can become prey. His camp gives travelers a place to pause before they enter the jungle depths.",sp=0},{t="The Hunt for Lar'korwi",b="Torwa Pathfinder spends much of his time tracking Lar'korwi, a fierce and cunning raptor in the crater's north. Brute strength alone will not bring down such a predator. He teaches hunters to study its feeding habits, then use fresh carcass meat and glands as bait to draw Lar'korwi into the open.",sp=0},{t="Primal Poisons and Beasts",b="Torwa Pathfinder studies poisonous plants and aggressive ape colonies, as well as the crater's raptors. He sends travelers to gather venom from volatile bloodpetals and watch powerful beasts such as U'cha, the mighty gorilla. Torwa seeks to understand how nature's deadliest defenses work in isolation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Torwa Pathfinder?",a="Torwa Pathfinder camps at Un'Goro Crater's eastern edge, near the foot of the winding ramp up to Tanaris.",al={"torwa location","where is torwa","find torwa pathfinder"}},{q="What is Lar'korwi?",a="Lar'korwi is a fierce and cunning raptor that roams Un'Goro Crater. Torwa teaches hunters to use bait made from fresh carcass meat and glands to draw it into the open.",al={"larkorwi","who is larkorwi","what is larkorwi"}},{q="Does Torwa only offer quests to Horde players?",a="No. Torwa Pathfinder offers his tracking wisdom and hunting challenges to capable adventurers of both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"is torwa horde only","can alliance talk to torwa","torwa faction"}},{q="Why is Torwa interested in Bloodpetals?",a="Torwa Pathfinder studies the lethal defenses of Un'Goro's native plants. He asks adventurers to gather secretions from aggressive bloodpetals so he can understand and test their natural toxins.",al={"bloodpetal quest","why bloodpetals","torwa poison"}},{q="Who is U'cha?",a="U'cha is a powerful gorilla living in Un'Goro's caves and ape territories. Torwa challenges hunters to defeat U'cha and prove their skill against the basin's strongest beasts.",al={"mighty u'cha","gorilla boss ungoro","ucha quest"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can learn from Torwa Pathfinder's patience and craft. To lure an apex predator, study its diet, scent, and territorial habits instead of relying on raw force.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may find Torwa Pathfinder's camp at the crater's edge a reassuring reminder of your people's reverence for nature amid Un'Goro's prehistoric wilds."},kw={"bloodpetal","lar'korwi","pathfinder","raptor","tanaris","torwa","u'cha","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","zone:tanaris","topic:tauren"},src={"Torwa Pathfinder"}}
E["npc:williden-marshal"] = {t="npc",n="Williden Marshal",z="ungoro",s="At Marshal's Refuge, Williden Marshal keeps his expedition alive after beasts drove it from Un'Goro Crater's lower camps. He still hopes the crater's plants, crystals and scientific research will bring discovery and profit.",h="At Marshal's Refuge, Williden Marshal keeps his expedition alive after beasts drove it from Un'Goro Crater's...",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="Williden Marshal brought a scientific expedition into Un'Goro Crater to seek discovery and fortune. Strange crystals, unrecorded plants and other resources drew him to the valley floor, where he set up several camps. The crater's beasts soon tore through the research posts. Williden and the survivors fled to the northern cliffs and made their base at Marshal's Refuge.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Dream",b="Williden refuses to abandon the expedition after losing its lower camps. From Marshal's Refuge, he asks travelers to search the lowlands for lost food crates, scientific instruments and his expedition journal. Close companions such as Spark Nilminer call him Wil, but Williden takes the work seriously. The expedition's research remains in the valley, beneath the paths of its great predators.",sp=0},{t="Family Ties",b="Hol'anyee Marshal works alongside Williden at Marshal's Refuge. The two Marshals chose the wild crater in southern Kalimdor for their expedition. Williden still believes Un'Goro's crystal deposits and ancient mysteries can bring them fortune.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Williden Marshal?",a="Williden Marshal leads Marshal's Expedition, a team of human researchers and adventurers in Un'Goro Crater. He brought them there to study its strange crystals and plants, hoping to gain knowledge and profit.",al={"who is williden marshal","williden marshal lore","who leads marshal's refuge"}},{q="Why is the expedition holed up in a cave?",a="The crater's great predators drove the expedition from its lower research camps in Un'Goro's lowlands. The survivors fled to the northern cliffs and now shelter at Marshal's Refuge.",al={"why is the refuge in a cave","what happened to the expedition camps","why did marshal retreat"}},{q="What is Williden asking adventurers to do?",a="Williden asks travelers to search the dangerous crater basin for supplies lost at the ruined camps. These include food, scientific instruments and his expedition journal.",al={"williden quests","expedition salvation","what does williden want"}},{q="What brought Williden to Un'Goro Crater in the first place?",a="Williden came to Un'Goro Crater for its rare plants, mysterious crystals and ancient geological secrets. He hopes scientific discoveries will bring profit back home.",al={"why come to ungoro","williden marshal motivation","what is marshal researching"}},{q="Does Williden have any family?",a="Yes. Hol'anyee Marshal is Williden's sister and works alongside him at Marshal's Refuge as part of the Marshal Expeditions.",al={"williden brother","livingston marshal","marshal family"}},{q="Is Williden Marshal aligned with the Alliance or Horde?",a="Williden leads a neutral scientific expedition from Marshal's Refuge. He accepts help from Alliance and Horde travelers willing to recover supplies and clear dangers from the crater.",al={"is williden alliance","can horde talk to williden","marshal refuge faction"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, Williden reflects humanity's curiosity and ambition. He traveled from the Eastern Kingdoms to the wilds of southern Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Williden's team working neutrally in the wild crater while keeping cultural and trade ties to the Alliance heartlands.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you may understand why Un'Goro's unusual prehistoric plants drew Williden's expedition to the crater."},kw={"devilsaurs","marshals expedition","marshals refuge","power crystals","spark nilminer","ungoro crater","williden marshal"},rel={"subzone:marshal-s-refuge","zone:ungoro","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Williden Marshal"}}
E["subzone:fire-plume-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Fire Plume Ridge",z="ungoro",s="Fire Plume Ridge burns at Un'Goro Crater's heart. Its magma warms the basin and feeds the geysers and steam pools. Fire elementals roam its slopes.",h="Fire Plume Ridge burns at Un'Goro Crater's heart.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Crater",b="Lava runs down Fire Plume Ridge into Un'Goro Crater's jungle basin. Beneath the rock, magma channels spread under the soil and feed the geysers and hot springs. The heat is fierce, so travelers climbing the ridge need water and shade.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Elementals",b="Fire elementals roam the glowing lava flows, drawn by the deep heat below the ridge. Blazerunner dwells in a cavern near the summit and rules Un'Goro's elementals. Those who climb toward the peak face scorching heat and spirits defending their fiery home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the volcano in the middle of Un'Goro Crater?",a="Fire Plume Ridge rises at the center of Un'Goro Crater. Its magma channels warm the basin and feed its geysers and steam springs.",al={"ungoro volcano name","volcano in center of ungoro","fire plume ridge location"}},{q="Who rules the elementals at Fire Plume Ridge?",a="Blazerunner rules Un'Goro's fire elementals from a cavern near the peak.",al={"boss of fire plume ridge","blazerunner location","fire elemental boss ungoro"}},{q="Why is there an explorer stranded inside the ridge?",a="Ringo, a goblin-allied adventurer, entered the volcano to explore. Severe heat exhaustion left him stranded in a southern cave, unable to escape alone.",al={"who is stranded in fire plume ridge","ringo ungoro","lost guy in volcano"}},{q="How does the volcano affect the rest of Un'Goro?",a="Magma channels run beneath Un'Goro's crater floor from Fire Plume Ridge. They warm the earth and feed the geysers, thermal vents, and steam pools.",al={"why is ungoro so hot","crater geothermal activity","shallow magma veins ungoro"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see fire spirits raging across the ridge. They reveal the elemental powers beneath Kalimdor's crust.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find exposed minerals in the ridge's crags and heat-hardened slopes. Dense Thorium formed there under volcanic pressure."},kw={"blazerunner","elementals","fire plume ridge","lava","ringo","ungoro","volcano"},rel={"zone:ungoro","npc:ringo"},src={"Fire Plume Ridge"}}
E["subzone:fungal-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Fungal Rock",z="ungoro",s="At Un'Goro Crater's northeastern cliff, gorillas make their den in Fungal Rock. Ghost Mushrooms grow in its damp passages, among the crater's most dangerous ape dens.",h="At Un'Goro Crater's northeastern cliff, gorillas make their den in Fungal Rock.",sec={{t="The Ape Den",b="A waterfall and pool mark Fungal Rock's entrance on Un'Goro Crater's northeastern edge. Massive gorillas make their den in the damp underground corridors. Un'Goro Stompers and Thunderers move among Ghost Mushrooms there. Deep inside, the silverback U'cha and the albino gorilla Uhk'loc hold their territory. Near the cave mouth, a curious traveler may find A-Me 01, a damaged mechanical ape abandoned by gnome researchers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fungal Rock?",a="Fungal Rock's damp passages cut into Un'Goro Crater's northeastern wall. Ghost Mushrooms grow among the hostile gorillas in its caves.",al={"where is fungal rock","what is fungal rock cave"}},{q="Who rules the apes inside Fungal Rock?",a="U'cha, a massive silverback, rules Fungal Rock's deepest chamber. The rare white gorilla Uhk'loc also roams the caverns.",al={"who is u'cha","boss of fungal rock","fungal rock leader"}},{q="Why is there a mechanical gorilla outside the cave?",a="A-Me 01 rests near the pool outside Fungal Rock's entrance. Dwarf researcher Karna Remtravel built the mechanical ape, which broke down during field observations and awaits salvage or repair.",al={"what is a-me 01","robot gorilla ungoro","ame 01"}},{q="What valuable resources grow in Fungal Rock?",a="Ghost Mushrooms grow in Fungal Rock's damp, shaded interior. It is one of the few places in southern Kalimdor where herbalists can gather this sought-after fungus.",al={"ghost mushrooms ungoro","herbs in fungal rock"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="At Fungal Rock, you can gather Ghost Mushrooms, though territorial gorillas guard the cavern passages.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may want to investigate A-Me 01, Karna Remtravel's mechanical ape prototype, left near the entrance pool."},kw={"a-me 01","crater","fungal rock","ghost mushroom","gorilla","u'cha","uhk'loc","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro"},src={"Fungal Rock"}}
E["subzone:golakka-hot-springs"] = {t="subzone",n="Golakka Hot Springs",z="ungoro",s="In western Un'Goro Crater, Golakka Hot Springs send geysers skyward north of Terror Run. Fire Plume Ridge's heat draws researchers and alchemists to the steaming pools.",h="In western Un'Goro Crater, Golakka Hot Springs send geysers skyward north of Terror Run.",sec={{t="Boiling Waters and Volcanic Steam",b="Golakka Hot Springs bubble north of Terror Run in western Un'Goro Crater. Heat from Fire Plume Ridge drives scalding water up through the ground. It leaves mineral terraces, and geysers break across the basin. Steaming Furies prowl the pools where groundwater meets volcanic heat. Explorers, herbalists, and researchers still come to study the crater's unusual geology.",sp=0},{t="Curious Inhabitants and Strange Chemistry",b="Alchemists prize Golakka's spring water as a strong catalyst. They use it even in delicate concoctions such as love potions. Spark Nilminer, a curious visitor, perches atop the central geyser vent. Researcher Krakle comes to study how the springs reach into the crater's volcanic heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the springs so hot?",a="Fire Plume Ridge's volcanic system heats the springs beneath Un'Goro Crater. Magma superheats underground water, sending boiling, mineral-rich water and steam through the geysers and terraced pools.",al={"why is water boiling","geothermal heat un'goro","fire plume connection"}},{q="What creatures live in Golakka Hot Springs?",a="Steaming Furies prowl the shores and pools. Volcanic heat transforms living water into roiling, volatile steam.",al={"hot springs elementals","what lives in golakka","steaming fury"}},{q="What is the water from the hot springs used for?",a="Alchemists and eccentric brewers value the water for its unusual chemical properties. Pristine spring water goes into special brews, including potent love potions.",al={"golakka water use","hot springs love potion","hot springs reagents"}},{q="Who is Krakle and what was he doing here?",a="Krakle studies the geothermal link between Golakka Hot Springs and Fire Plume Ridge. He gathers observations and temperature readings around the springs.",al={"krakle un'goro","krakle hot springs","researcher at the hot springs"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may share Spark Nilminer's fascination with the fierce geology here. He braves the scalding pressure vents to watch geothermal forces at work.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see fire and water clash in the hot springs. Their meeting gives rise to boiling Steaming Furies along the mineral banks."},kw={"fire plume ridge","geyser","golakka","hot springs","krakle","spark nilminer","steaming fury","terror run","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:terror-run"},src={"Golakka Hot Springs"}}
E["subzone:lakkari-tar-pits"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakkari Tar Pits",z="ungoro",s="In northern Un’Goro Crater, the Lakkari Tar Pits hold beasts fast and give rise to hostile tar elementals.",h="In northern Un’Goro Crater, the Lakkari Tar Pits hold beasts fast and give rise to hostile tar elementals.",sec={{t="A Grasping Trap",b="South of Marshal’s Refuge, the Lakkari Tar Pits spread across northern Un’Goro Crater. Their black tar grips anyone who steps in and drags beasts and travelers into the mire. Bones of countless prehistoric creatures jut through the surface. Scavengers circle the pools for trapped prey, while tar beasts, lurkers, and creepers rise from the muck to attack those who enter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens if you step into the tar?",a="The tar grips anyone who wades in, slowing them to a crawl. That makes escape difficult when aggressive tar elementals patrol the pools.",al={"tar pits effect","tar slow","stepping in tar"}},{q="What creatures live in the Lakkari Tar Pits?",a="Tar beasts, tar creepers, tar lurkers, and tar lords inhabit the pits. Local scavengers circle the pools, searching for trapped prey.",al={"tar beasts","tar pit monsters","tar creepers"}},{q="Where are the Lakkari Tar Pits located?",a="The Lakkari Tar Pits lie in northern Un’Goro Crater, in the basin directly below the cliffs of Marshal’s Refuge.",al={"tar pits location","where is lakkari","how to find tar pits"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, keep your pets on firm ground near Lakkari. Creatures caught in the thick sludge make easy prey for tar lurkers."},kw={"creeper","lakkari","marshal's refuge","tar beast","tar pits","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:marshal-s-refuge"},src={"Lakkari Tar Pits"}}
E["subzone:marshal-s-refuge"] = {t="subzone",n="Marshal's Refuge",z="ungoro",s="In Marshal's Refuge, expedition survivors shelter above Un'Goro Crater's dangerous basin. Williden Marshal and his party established the camp after beasts overran their lower camps.",h="In Marshal's Refuge, expedition survivors shelter above Un'Goro Crater's dangerous basin.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Williden and Hol'anyee Marshal led their expedition into Un'Goro Crater. Its ancient beasts proved fiercer than they expected. After the creatures overran their first camps again and again, the survivors fled to the northern cliffs. Now Marshal's Refuge clings to a cavernous ledge above the jungle floor, where weary explorers can rest, find basic supplies, and speak with flight masters.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads of Curiosity",b="Researchers and wanderers gather at Marshal's Refuge to study Un'Goro Crater's ancient life and strange crystals. The surviving Marshal crew shares the crowded ledge with naturalists from many lands, including dwarven scholars and gnomish tinkerers. From the camp, scouts set out for Fire Plume Ridge and the Golakka Hot Springs. They hope to record the wilderness before it overwhelms them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Marshal's Refuge built so high up the cliff?",a="Un'Goro's fierce beasts repeatedly overran the expedition's lower camps. The survivors retreated to the northern cliffs, where the rock wall gave them a defensible perch beyond the reach of larger creatures.",al={"why is it in a cave","marshals refuge location","why cliffside camp"}},{q="Is Marshal's Refuge friendly to both Horde and Alliance?",a="Yes. Marshal's Refuge is a neutral outpost where members of both factions can mingle, resupply, and trade research.",al={"is marshals refuge neutral","can horde go here","can alliance go here"}},{q="Who leads the encampment?",a="Williden Marshal and Hol'anyee Marshal lead the encampment. They organized the Marshal Expeditions into Un'Goro Crater.",al={"who is in charge","who runs marshals refuge","camp leader"}},{q="What services are available at the Refuge?",a="The Refuge has a flight master, basic trade merchants, and repair services. Researchers also gather there to offer bounties and investigations across the crater.",al={"flight path","repairs","vendors"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can study Un'Goro's rare and deadly beasts from the Refuge's perch before heading down to track them.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can use the Refuge as an outpost to test apparatus on Un'Goro's strange power crystals and volatile geysers."},kw={"cave","expedition","hol'anyee","marshal's refuge","un'goro crater","williden marshal"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:golakka-hot-springs","topic:gnome","topic:dwarf"},src={"Marshal's Refuge"}}
E["subzone:marshlands"] = {t="subzone",n="Marshlands",z="ungoro",s="The Tanaris trail brings travelers into Un'Goro through the Marshlands. Raptors hunt among the wetlands, where Blue Power Crystals lie scattered and two wilderness experts keep apart.",h="The Tanaris trail brings travelers into Un'Goro through the Marshlands.",sec={{t="Gateway to the Crater",b="From Tanaris, the trail descends into the Marshlands. It is the only safe way down Un'Goro's sheer crater rim. Dense canopies, standing water, and mud conceal packs of fierce raptors. Some are venomous hunters that stalk the reeds. Blue Power Crystals, found nowhere else in Un'Goro, lie across damp clearings.",sp=0},{t="Encampments in the Bog",b="Several wilderness experts keep solitary outposts in the dangerous marsh. Torwa Pathfinder, a tauren hunter, watches the primeval fauna from a prominent earthen mound. Across the wetlands, Mor'vek studies and trains native ravasaurs. Mor'vek is a troll.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Marshlands usually the first area people see in Un'Goro?",a="Un'Goro's sheer crater cliffs make any approach beyond the southeastern pass from Tanaris almost certainly fatal. The descending ramp leads into the Marshlands, so travelers on foot pass through its wetlands.",al={"how to enter ungoro","entering ungoro crater","marshlands entrance"}},{q="What creatures are most common here?",a="Raptors fill the Marshlands, from ordinary hunters to venomous kinds that stalk the thick brush.",al={"marshlands beasts","marshlands raptors","what lives here"}},{q="What unique resources are found in the Marshlands?",a="Blue Power Crystals form naturally only in the Marshlands. Researchers prize them for studying the mysterious crystalline pylons scattered through the basin.",al={"blue power crystals","marshlands crystals","blue crystals ungoro"}},{q="Who is Torwa Pathfinder?",a="Torwa Pathfinder is a tauren hunter who watches Un'Goro's fauna from a prominent mound in the Marshlands.",al={"torwa","torwa pathfinder camp"}},{q="Can the ravasaurs here be tamed or trained?",a="Yes. Mor'vek is a troll based across the wetlands who studies and trains native ravasaurs.",al={"ravasaur trainer","morvek","train ravasaur"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your wilderness skills against swift raptors, venomous predators, and rare beasts. Torwa Pathfinder watches the local fauna.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can find aggressive bloodpetal saplings and damp foliage along the marsh's northern edges. The plants here are hostile and mobile."},kw={"blue power crystals","marshlands","mor'vek","raptors","ravasaur","tanaris","torwa pathfinder","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","zone:tanaris","npc:torwa-pathfinder"},src={"Marshlands"}}
E["subzone:shaper-s-terrace"] = {t="subzone",n="Shaper's Terrace",z="ungoro",s="High above Marshal's Refuge, Shaper's Terrace bears the mark of the ancient titans. Its overlook honors Khaz'goroth the Shaper and recalls the experiments that shaped Un'Goro Crater.",h="High above Marshal's Refuge, Shaper's Terrace bears the mark of the ancient titans.",sec={{t="A Legacy of the Titans",b="From the northern bluffs, Shaper's Terrace looks across Un'Goro Crater. Monumental stone works left by the titans crown the high plateau. The site is believed to honor Khaz'goroth the Shaper, one of the celestial architects who cultivated the crater as a living laboratory for early life on Azeroth.\n\nFrom these heights, ancient entities once watched and directed the flora and fauna below. Stone arches and massive metallic plinths still rise above the wilderness thriving beneath them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shaper's Terrace?",a="Shaper's Terrace rises along the northern bluffs of Un'Goro Crater, directly above Marshal's Refuge. Its stone structures were left by the titans who shaped the land.",al={"shapers terrace","what is this terrace","ungoro terrace"}},{q="Who was the 'Shaper'?",a="The Shaper was Khaz'goroth, one of the titanic creators who helped craft and cultivate Azeroth in the deep past.",al={"who is the shaper","khazgoroth","who made shapers terrace"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see another glimpse of Khaz'goroth's architecture and the grand works of the creators at Shaper's Terrace."},kw={"crater","khaz'goroth","marshal's refuge","shaper","shaper's terrace","titan","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:marshal-s-refuge","topic:titan"},src={"Shaper's Terrace"}}
E["subzone:slithering-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Slithering Scar",z="ungoro",s="In southern Un'Goro, the Gorishi swarm presses into the crater. Their hive tunnels through the cliffs and threatens life in the basin.",h="In southern Un'Goro, the Gorishi swarm presses into the crater.",sec={{t="The Gorishi Hive",b="In southern Un'Goro, the Gorishi hive cuts into the cliffs. This organized strain of silithid has burrows and egg chambers through the rock. Workers and tunnelers tend eggs and grubs, while towering wasp broods fill the warrens below.\n\nThe colony also raises fledgling silithid colossi, behemoths meant to carve an uncontested path through the crater's ecology. Strange crystals pulse inside the hive with an unnatural resonance, focusing the colony's dark, coordinated will.",sp=0},{t="A Missing Ward",b="Scholars and explorers crossing Un'Goro's perimeter find no ancient crystalline pylon on its southern boundary. Pylons stand sentinel along the basin's northern, eastern, and western edges. Through this unprotected gap, the Gorishi have burrowed inward from the neighboring deserts.\n\nDid the silithid undermine a forgotten southern ward, or enter where the crater's primordial wards were weakest? Those watching the swarm's rapid expansion have no answer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Slithering Scar?",a="The Gorishi swarm inhabits a hive complex carved into Un'Goro Crater's southern cliff walls.",al={"what is this place","slithering scar overview","ungoro bug hive"}},{q="What are the silithid doing here?",a="The Gorishi dig vast underground tunnels, tend nursery chambers filled with grubs and eggs, and raise massive silithid colossi to establish dominance over the crater.",al={"why are bugs here","silithid purpose ungoro","gorishi goal"}},{q="Why is there no pylon in the south like the other regions?",a="Ancient crystal pylons mark Un'Goro's northern, eastern, and western edges, but none stands on the southern cliffs. The Slithering Scar emerged where this protective boundary is missing.",al={"missing southern pylon","why no south pylon","where is the south pylon"}},{q="What dangerous creatures inhabit the hive?",a="Workers, reavers, and stingers inhabit the Scar, along with developing colossi and ferocious broodmothers such as Clutchmother Zavas.",al={"hive bosses","notable bugs","clutchmother zavas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see how the Gorishi hive's aggressive spread threatens the crater's untamed vitality. Stay vigilant against this unnatural infestation."},kw={"clutchmother zavas","colossus","gorishi","hive","silithid","slithering scar","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","npc:grub"},src={"Slithering Scar"}}
E["subzone:terror-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Terror Run",z="ungoro",s="In Terror Run, predators stalk the open shelf beneath Un'Goro Crater's southwestern rim. The land lies west of the Slithering Scar, with devilsaurs and diemetradons below and pterrordax overhead.",h="In Terror Run, predators stalk the open shelf beneath Un'Goro Crater's southwestern rim.",sec={{t="A Hunt in the Open",b="Beneath Un'Goro Crater's mountainous rim, Terror Run spreads across the southwestern shelf. Pterrordax wheel overhead as diemetradons, stegodons, and apex devilsaurs roam the low brush. The Slithering Scar's strange mounds lie close by.\n\nAlong Terror Run's eastern edge, the ruins of a camp mark where Williden Marshal's expedition was caught unprepared. The crater's primeval predators closed in before they could escape.",sp=0},{t="Red Crystals and Ancient Predators",b="Naturalists and adventurers come to Terror Run for Red Power Crystals, which rise from its fertile soil. Their crimson formations hum with primeval energy, like the blue, green, and yellow crystals found elsewhere in the basin.\n\nYet gathering them means facing the plains' strongest hunters. Apex devilsaurs nest in the deep south and brook no trespassers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called Terror Run?",a="Terror Run takes its name from the many apex predators roaming its open corridor. Massive devilsaurs and territorial diemetradons prowl the flats while pterrordax watch from above. Anyone crossing on foot may have to sprint for their life.",al={"terror run name meaning","why terror run","who named terror run"}},{q="What can be found here besides dangerous beasts?",a="Red Power Crystals rise from the earth only in Terror Run. On the eastern edge, you can also find an abandoned research camp from Williden Marshal's expedition, left behind during its dangerous survey of the crater.",al={"what is in terror run","terror run crystals","terror run resources"}},{q="What is the abandoned camp on the eastern edge?",a="The abandoned campsite belonged to members of Williden Marshal's expedition. Scientists and explorers left their research equipment and fled when local wildlife overwhelmed their position.",al={"marshals camp terror run","abandoned research camp","lost expedition camp"}},{q="Where does Terror Run lie in relation to other landmarks?",a="Terror Run spans southwestern Un'Goro Crater, directly west of the silithid-infested hives of the Slithering Scar and south of the central volcano, Fire Plume Ridge.",al={"terror run location","where is terror run"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find some of Kalimdor's fiercest beasts across Terror Run's vast plains, from swift raptors and savage pterrordax to towering devilsaurs."},kw={"devilsaur","diemetradon","marshal expedition","pterrordax","red power crystal","slithering scar","terror run","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:slithering-scar"},src={"Terror Run"}}
E["zone:ungoro"] = {t="zone",n="Un'Goro Crater",z="ungoro",s="Un'Goro Crater draws travelers into a lush basin between the deserts of Tanaris and Silithus. Dinosaurs roam beneath a central volcano, among living elementals and ancient Titan relics. Colored power crystals lie across the basin, though their origins remain a mystery.",h="Un'Goro Crater draws travelers into a lush basin between the deserts of Tanaris and Silithus.",sec={{t="The God Lands",b="Ancient night elf records of the War of the Shifting Sands say the Qiraji were turned back at Un'Goro Crater's edges. In their tongue, they called this place the 'God Lands.' Scholars believe the Titans may have used the caldera as a testing ground or dwelling while shaping Kalimdor. Stone pylons rise along the ridges and hum with energy. Blue, red, green, and yellow crystals emerge from the primeval earth.",sp=0},{t="A Savage Ecosystem",b="Un'Goro has no cities, towns, or native humanoid societies. Life thrives here in a wild, primeval state. Devilsaurs stalk the flats of Terror Run, bloodpetals lash out in the marshlands, and oozes creep across the tar pits of Lakkari. At the crater's heart, Fire Plume Ridge is an active volcano filled with hostile fire elementals led by Blazerunner. Explorers and skinners seek its natural wealth, including devilsaur hides, if they can survive the food chain.",sp=0},{t="Marshal's Refuge",b="Marshal's Refuge, an elevated camp in the northern cliffs, holds nearly all of Un'Goro's settled presence. Williden Marshal led scientists, naturalists, and fortune seekers here to catalogue the basin's treasures.\n\nMonstrous wildlife battered the expedition and drove its members to high ground. The refuge remains an embattled staging ground for travelers studying the mysterious power crystals, mapping volcanic activity, and watching silithid swarms encroach through the southern ridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into Un'Goro Crater?",a="Natural ramps lead down the crater walls. One comes from southwestern Tanaris near Thistleshrub Valley, and another from northeastern Silithus. Without magical aid, a leap from the cliffs is fatal. Marshal's Refuge in the north has flight connections to Gadgetzan and Cenarion Hold.",al={"how to enter ungoro","ungoro entrance","how to reach ungoro crater"}},{q="What are the colored power crystals used for?",a="Red, blue, green, and yellow Power Crystals lie across the jungle floor. Gnome researcher J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge can guide explorers in deciphering how to use them at the Northern, Eastern, and Western Pylons. Combine certain colors at the right pylons to harness latent Titan energies and make defensive or restorative charms.",al={"ungoro crystals","red blue green yellow crystals ungoro","power pylons"}},{q="Why is Un'Goro lush despite being surrounded by deserts?",a="Scholars believe the Titans, who shaped the world, made Un'Goro's unnatural vibrancy. Titanic conduits, warmth from Fire Plume Ridge, and ancient ley energy nourish its isolated, fast-growing ecosystem. It resists the arid conditions of neighboring Tanaris and Silithus.",al={"why is ungoro a jungle","ungoro desert connection","how does ungoro have plants"}},{q="Why did the Qiraji call this place the 'God Lands'?",a="Tablets translated from the War of the Shifting Sands say the insect swarms halted at Un'Goro's threshold. In their tongue, they called it the 'God Lands.' Geologist Larksbane, who translated the account, connects the name to theories that the Titans once dwelt in the crater and wonders whether Aman'Thul himself watched over it.",al={"god lands meaning","qiraji ungoro","why couldn't silithid take ungoro"}},{q="What is Un'Goro Soil used for?",a="Rich, potent dirt lies across the crater basin. Pair harvested soil with Tharlendris seeds in an Evergreen Pouch to grow Morrowgrain, a mystical herb intensely sought by researchers in Thunder Bluff, Darnassus, and the Cenarion Circle.",al={"ungoro soil sample","what does ungoro soil do","morrowgrain soil"}},{q="Are there any humanoid settlements or dungeons here?",a="Un'Goro Crater has the Shaper's Terrace, for those around 58 to 60, but no indigenous humanoid societies. Marshal's Refuge, a small expedition outpost on the northern rim, is the only lasting settlement. Aside from isolated hermit hunters or lost explorers, the caldera is entirely wild.",al={"ungoro dungeons","who lives in ungoro","humanoids in ungoro"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The basin's rich moisture lets Blindweed, Dreamfoil, and Golden Sansam flourish alongside Firebloom on the volcano's slopes. Few places in Kalimdor have all four growing together.",["profession:Mining"]="Mithril Deposits and Rich Thorium Veins are dense along the crater walls and the crags of Fire Plume Ridge. Un'Goro is a premier destination for high-end ore.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can study Un'Goro's isolated ecosystem with the Cenarion Circle and harvest its rich soil to grow Morrowgrain. The Circle seeks to understand the pure, untamed life force that sustains the caldera.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance naturalist, you can gather with Williden Marshal and J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge. Alliance naturalists race to decipher the Titan pylons while protecting Darnassus researchers who collect soil samples.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you can come through Tanaris to test your prowess against legendary devilsaurs. You can also help Thunder Bluff herbalists cultivate Morrowgrain from Un'Goro's primeval dirt."},kw={"devilsaur","fire plume ridge","god lands","lakkari","marshal's refuge","power crystals","torwa pathfinder","ungoro","ungoro crater"},rel={"subzone:marshal-s-refuge","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:lakkari-tar-pits","subzone:terror-run","zone:tanaris","zone:silithus","npc:williden-marshal","topic:titan"},src={"Un'Goro Crater (Classic)","Un'Goro Crater"}}
